1
00:00:02,135 --> 00:00:03,403
EPISODE 5

2
00:00:08,342 --> 00:00:10,177
Hey, hey, hey!

3
00:00:10,244 --> 00:00:12,079
Hey, wake up!

4
00:00:12,145 --> 00:00:14,281
I said wake up!

5
00:00:14,348 --> 00:00:16,817
Look at these grown men.

6
00:00:16,884 --> 00:00:19,119
Passed out from makgeolli? Really?

7
00:00:19,186 --> 00:00:21,355
Ugh, what fragile little punks.

8
00:00:22,756 --> 00:00:25,158
Still, I heard Min-gi

9
00:00:25,225 --> 00:00:28,362
helped the villagers with their work

10
00:00:28,428 --> 00:00:31,265
and begged them to come to practice.

11
00:00:32,165 --> 00:00:35,435
-Isn't that admirable?
-After all the stunts he pulled,

12
00:00:35,502 --> 00:00:39,239
it barely makes a dent,
but it is pretty admirable.

13
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:42,543
Oh, gosh, where is my head?

14
00:00:42,609 --> 00:00:44,411
It's time to feed the cows.

15
00:00:48,549 --> 00:00:49,683
Gosh.

16
00:01:30,958 --> 00:01:32,826
What are you doing here?

17
00:01:33,393 --> 00:01:34,995
Oh…

18
00:01:35,062 --> 00:01:38,131
I just saw the piano here.

19
00:01:38,198 --> 00:01:40,968
Why keep such a nice piano out here?

20
00:01:41,034 --> 00:01:43,737
That's none of your business.

21
00:01:43,804 --> 00:01:45,639
Anyway, you're pretty good.

22
00:01:45,706 --> 00:01:47,908
Look at you, playing classical too…

23
00:01:50,444 --> 00:01:54,047
-I learned it from my girlfriend.
-Whoa, you even have a girlfriend?

24
00:01:54,114 --> 00:01:56,483
Does she know you're living like this?

25
00:01:56,550 --> 00:01:58,452
Well…

26
00:02:01,588 --> 00:02:02,823
She died.

27
00:02:04,958 --> 00:02:06,927
Eight years ago.

28
00:02:06,994 --> 00:02:10,998
And she looked so much like you.

29
00:02:12,032 --> 00:02:15,068
Your eyes, your nose,

30
00:02:16,269 --> 00:02:19,906
your lips, even your voice.

31
00:02:23,477 --> 00:02:25,512
So whenever I look at you…

32
00:02:27,714 --> 00:02:29,883
I think of her.

33
00:02:33,053 --> 00:02:35,489
I keep falling for you…

34
00:02:37,457 --> 00:02:38,625
What should I do?

35
00:02:44,865 --> 00:02:46,133
You fell for it, right?

36
00:02:46,199 --> 00:02:48,335
I was just joking.

37
00:02:49,770 --> 00:02:51,638
You were joking?

38
00:02:51,705 --> 00:02:53,573
Gosh, what a disappointment.

39
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:57,144
I thought I might get to live
with an energetic younger husband.

40
00:02:57,210 --> 00:03:00,113
Wow, you never let anything slide.

41
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:02,482
Play the piano too.
I heard you're good.

42
00:03:02,549 --> 00:03:05,152
I don't play the piano anymore.

43
00:03:05,218 --> 00:03:07,287
Whenever I sit at the piano,

44
00:03:08,055 --> 00:03:10,023
I think of him.

45
00:03:10,724 --> 00:03:13,393
-Him?
-The man I loved

46
00:03:14,061 --> 00:03:16,697
more than my own life.

47
00:03:18,465 --> 00:03:19,933
But…

48
00:03:22,235 --> 00:03:24,204
he went far away,

49
00:03:26,606 --> 00:03:30,243
somewhere I can never see him again.

50
00:03:32,512 --> 00:03:33,847
Oh…

51
00:03:34,681 --> 00:03:36,183
I see.

52
00:03:37,584 --> 00:03:40,053
Just kidding! Did you fall for it?

53
00:03:43,423 --> 00:03:45,992
You're no match for me no matter what.

54
00:03:46,059 --> 00:03:48,195
Go on inside and get some sleep.

55
00:03:49,830 --> 00:03:51,732
Huh? Why are you laughing?

56
00:03:51,798 --> 00:03:54,134
-Am I funny to you?
-No.

57
00:03:54,201 --> 00:03:56,703
You really crack my head up.

58
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:02,809
Ow, why did you hit me?

59
00:04:02,876 --> 00:04:04,077
You said to crack it!

60
00:04:04,144 --> 00:04:06,279
Want a few more? I'll smack you good!

61
00:04:06,346 --> 00:04:08,615
Little brat acting all cheeky, jeez.

62
00:04:14,554 --> 00:04:17,190
Would you like me to help?

63
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:19,159
No, I'm fine. Go back down.

64
00:04:19,226 --> 00:04:21,094
Come on, let me help you out.

65
00:04:21,161 --> 00:04:22,596
I told you I'm fine.

66
00:04:22,662 --> 00:04:24,664
I just give them fodder like this.

67
00:04:24,731 --> 00:04:28,935
Hey, don't make more work! Seriously!

68
00:04:29,002 --> 00:04:31,138
-Eat up.
-Honestly, I swear…

69
00:04:31,204 --> 00:04:33,673
-It's good, come here.
-She only eats from Mom.

70
00:04:33,740 --> 00:04:35,142
Come here, over here.

71
00:04:36,076 --> 00:04:37,477
Eat up.

72
00:04:37,544 --> 00:04:41,348
I told you to go back down.
I can handle it myself today.

73
00:04:47,354 --> 00:04:50,824
25TH SOUL-MYEON RESIDENTS' SPORTS DAY

74
00:04:53,827 --> 00:04:56,129
SOUL-MYEON SPORTS DAY CHAMPION

75
00:04:58,365 --> 00:05:01,802
Wow, it's pretty grand
for a country sports day.

76
00:05:01,868 --> 00:05:05,972
I know. The look in their eyes
puts Olympic athletes to shame.

77
00:05:06,039 --> 00:05:08,275
Jeez, this is making me nervous.

78
00:05:08,875 --> 00:05:12,612
Hey, don't be nervous.
They're just old country geezers.

79
00:05:12,679 --> 00:05:14,981
Nervous, my foot. Don't even worry.

80
00:05:18,718 --> 00:05:20,420
Seriously…

81
00:05:21,755 --> 00:05:23,323
Hey! Perk up.

82
00:05:23,390 --> 00:05:25,258
If we don't win, we get kicked out!

83
00:05:25,325 --> 00:05:27,327
I'm not in the mood for that.

84
00:05:30,864 --> 00:05:32,465
-What's with you?
-Hold still.

85
00:05:32,532 --> 00:05:34,534
What are you doing? Let go!

86
00:05:34,601 --> 00:05:37,037
-The young lady came too?
-That's right.

87
00:05:37,103 --> 00:05:39,673
She was painting in town,
so I dragged her here.

88
00:05:39,739 --> 00:05:42,409
Making all this fuss
when nobody's even there…

89
00:05:42,475 --> 00:05:44,878
-Ow!
-I really have work to do.

90
00:05:44,945 --> 00:05:46,947
Could I just leave right now?

91
00:05:47,013 --> 00:05:50,083
Tut-tut! Where would you go
on such an important day?

92
00:05:51,384 --> 00:05:54,154
I see them over there.

93
00:05:54,221 --> 00:05:56,957
We have to cheer on a day like today!

94
00:05:57,958 --> 00:05:59,326
Jeez.

95
00:06:01,361 --> 00:06:04,798
It's over. It's all over.

96
00:06:05,298 --> 00:06:07,133
She'll hate the sight of me.

97
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:10,203
I made a fool of myself
not just once, but twice.

98
00:06:12,172 --> 00:06:14,474
Hey, get a grip! Snap out of it!

99
00:06:14,541 --> 00:06:18,011
We have to win no matter what
so we don't get kicked out.

100
00:06:18,078 --> 00:06:20,380
Why did that woman have to come here?

101
00:06:20,447 --> 00:06:22,148
Why ruin my mood, seriously?

102
00:06:22,215 --> 00:06:24,117
Are you in a bad mood?

103
00:06:24,184 --> 00:06:26,620
Don't worry, you've got us!

104
00:06:26,686 --> 00:06:29,723
Hadurok! Hadurok!

105
00:06:29,789 --> 00:06:34,160
No retreat! Crush them fast! Victory!

106
00:06:34,227 --> 00:06:35,996
But who's that foreign woman?

107
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:37,731
No idea, her body is killer.

108
00:06:37,797 --> 00:06:40,000
I know. And her chest…

109
00:06:41,134 --> 00:06:43,570
Right, sir? Her chest is…

110
00:06:43,637 --> 00:06:47,007
Well, my wife's chest sure is big.

111
00:06:47,607 --> 00:06:50,343
-Excuse me?
-I said it's big.

112
00:06:51,912 --> 00:06:53,780
Why, you little bastards!

113
00:06:53,847 --> 00:06:55,749
What's that about my wife's chest?

114
00:06:55,815 --> 00:06:57,117
I'll tear you punks…

115
00:06:57,183 --> 00:06:58,952
-We didn't know.
-Calm down, sir.

116
00:06:59,019 --> 00:07:00,353
We really didn't know.

117
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:03,423
Stop, Dad. Don't fight.

118
00:07:03,990 --> 00:07:07,861
Oh, hey there, son! I'm not fighting.

119
00:07:07,928 --> 00:07:11,231
I'm just playing with these big boys!

120
00:07:11,298 --> 00:07:13,300
Dad, don't fight.

121
00:07:13,366 --> 00:07:16,303
I'm not fighting. Want to go see Mom?

122
00:07:24,277 --> 00:07:28,248
What's with that pretty boy
who looks like a mini Tom Cruise?

123
00:07:28,315 --> 00:07:29,816
-He called him Dad.
-His dad?

124
00:07:29,883 --> 00:07:31,718
You're so sexy, honey.

125
00:07:31,785 --> 00:07:33,086
Come on, let's go.

126
00:07:33,153 --> 00:07:35,188
Aw, there's my sweet boy.

127
00:07:35,255 --> 00:07:38,058
Hey, doesn't that picture look weird?

128
00:07:38,124 --> 00:07:40,660
The kid got concentrated divine grace.

129
00:07:40,727 --> 00:07:44,731
The 25th Soul-myeon Sports Day
opening ceremony is about to begin.

130
00:07:44,798 --> 00:07:46,099
It's finally starting.

131
00:07:46,166 --> 00:07:48,835
-Please gather on the field.
-Let's go.

132
00:07:55,208 --> 00:07:58,912
For the past nine years,
I've had one dream every day.

133
00:07:58,979 --> 00:08:01,348
At the Soul-myeon Sports Day,

134
00:08:01,414 --> 00:08:02,749
we beat Sangdurok-ri,

135
00:08:02,816 --> 00:08:05,552
and Hadurok-ri lifts the trophy.

136
00:08:05,618 --> 00:08:08,088
Everyone, please give it your all.

137
00:08:08,154 --> 00:08:11,024
All right, shall we do a cheer?

138
00:08:14,127 --> 00:08:16,463
Let's go, Hadurok-ri!

139
00:08:16,529 --> 00:08:17,731
Let's go!

140
00:08:29,909 --> 00:08:32,145
Is he the Sangdurok-ri Village Head?

141
00:08:32,212 --> 00:08:33,580
Yes.

142
00:08:37,183 --> 00:08:39,319
Are you all marching off to war?

143
00:08:39,386 --> 00:08:41,221
Those glares are mighty fierce.

144
00:08:41,287 --> 00:08:42,889
At this sports day,

145
00:08:42,956 --> 00:08:45,291
we're going to win, so take note.

146
00:08:45,358 --> 00:08:46,826
Ha!

147
00:08:48,194 --> 00:08:49,963
Oh my, that's so terrifying

148
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:52,232
my knees are shaking with fear.

149
00:08:55,535 --> 00:08:57,404
Today, I'll show you

150
00:08:57,470 --> 00:09:00,673
that in this world,
willpower alone isn't enough.

151
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:03,476
I'll make you learn that the hard way.

152
00:09:09,716 --> 00:09:11,284
What is wrong with that jerk?

153
00:09:11,351 --> 00:09:13,853
That guy was fine before the army.

154
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:16,056
He's been batshit since he got back.

155
00:09:16,122 --> 00:09:18,558
I heard he hurt his frontal lobe
in the army.

156
00:09:18,625 --> 00:09:20,593
Forget it, forget it. Ignore him.

157
00:09:20,660 --> 00:09:22,128
Let's just go warm up.

158
00:09:22,195 --> 00:09:24,064
Let's go, let's go!

159
00:09:30,236 --> 00:09:31,738
Jeez…

160
00:09:33,673 --> 00:09:35,075
Hey.

161
00:09:36,743 --> 00:09:38,378
-Hey!
-Ow!

162
00:09:39,379 --> 00:09:41,181
-What's wrong?
-Ugh…

163
00:09:41,247 --> 00:09:43,383
-What? What is it?
-You crazy bastard!

164
00:09:43,450 --> 00:09:46,052
The puppy bit me right here!

165
00:09:47,087 --> 00:09:49,789
Right here? Sorry, man.

166
00:09:49,856 --> 00:09:51,925
Why'd you let a puppy bite your nipple…

167
00:09:51,991 --> 00:09:53,026
Shut up!

168
00:09:53,093 --> 00:09:56,729
Stop bringing up things
I don't want to think about, damn it.

169
00:09:56,796 --> 00:09:58,198
25TH SOUL-MYEON SPORTS DAY

170
00:09:58,264 --> 00:10:00,133
Dear residents of Soul-myeon,

171
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:02,435
despite the busy farming season,

172
00:10:02,502 --> 00:10:05,939
you have come to grace
the 25th Soul-myeon Sports Day

173
00:10:06,005 --> 00:10:09,609
with your presence
and attend this event today,

174
00:10:09,676 --> 00:10:12,645
and for that, I sincerely thank you.

175
00:10:12,712 --> 00:10:15,348
Now then, I officially declare

176
00:10:15,415 --> 00:10:18,518
the 25th Soul-myeon Sports Day open!

177
00:10:22,989 --> 00:10:25,859
We will now begin today's first event.

178
00:10:25,925 --> 00:10:28,428
Players for the first event,
Rubber Shoe Toss,

179
00:10:28,495 --> 00:10:30,563
please gather in front of the stage.

180
00:10:39,939 --> 00:10:41,841
SANGDUROK-RI

181
00:10:44,077 --> 00:10:45,912
17.9 cm.

182
00:10:45,979 --> 00:10:50,049
-I've got this!
-Ma'am, remember what I told you?

183
00:10:51,351 --> 00:10:53,887
The left foot is just for support.

184
00:10:53,953 --> 00:10:55,655
Come on, come on!

185
00:10:59,859 --> 00:11:01,094
Yes!

186
00:11:01,961 --> 00:11:03,396
HADUROK-RI

187
00:11:03,463 --> 00:11:04,797
Nice shot!

188
00:11:07,567 --> 00:11:10,370
By 30 cm, the winner is Hadurok-ri!

189
00:11:12,038 --> 00:11:14,607
WIN

190
00:11:40,166 --> 00:11:43,303
Win just this once, just once!

191
00:11:44,037 --> 00:11:45,238
One more!

192
00:11:57,016 --> 00:11:58,351
WIN

193
00:12:02,956 --> 00:12:06,459
Starting now, between Sangdurok-ri
and Hadurok-ri,

194
00:12:06,526 --> 00:12:09,295
we will begin the Yut Nori finals.

195
00:12:10,029 --> 00:12:12,065
We'll flip a coin for first turn--

196
00:12:12,131 --> 00:12:14,968
No need. Youth should defer to elders.

197
00:12:15,034 --> 00:12:16,736
Since I'm young, I'll yield it.

198
00:12:16,803 --> 00:12:18,471
You don't need to do that.

199
00:12:18,538 --> 00:12:20,540
Anyway, thanks.

200
00:12:20,607 --> 00:12:22,242
Here you are, sir.

201
00:12:28,581 --> 00:12:29,749
Hup!

202
00:12:33,086 --> 00:12:34,687
It's a mo!

203
00:12:34,754 --> 00:12:37,390
Since it's a mo,
you get another throw, sir.

204
00:12:37,457 --> 00:12:39,292
Hup!

205
00:12:40,393 --> 00:12:42,228
That's two mos in a row!

206
00:12:42,295 --> 00:12:44,497
-How do we move the pieces?
-Stack them.

207
00:12:45,732 --> 00:12:48,368
Grandpa, to be safe,
maybe move one piece first…

208
00:12:48,434 --> 00:12:49,702
-Stack them.
-Yes.

209
00:12:50,937 --> 00:12:52,538
Hup!

210
00:12:53,072 --> 00:12:54,607
Three mos in a row!

211
00:12:54,674 --> 00:12:55,608
Stack them.

212
00:12:55,675 --> 00:12:57,243
Grandpa, this is a huge risk!

213
00:12:57,310 --> 00:12:58,244
-Stack them.
-Yes.

214
00:12:58,311 --> 00:13:00,246
Hup!

215
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:03,316
What about your pieces, sir?

216
00:13:03,383 --> 00:13:05,485
Stack them. Hup!

217
00:13:07,153 --> 00:13:08,421
What is this?

218
00:13:09,022 --> 00:13:10,390
Hup!

219
00:13:11,324 --> 00:13:12,959
Another mo!

220
00:13:14,093 --> 00:13:15,995
Stack them.

221
00:13:16,062 --> 00:13:16,929
Hup!

222
00:13:18,998 --> 00:13:20,633
Seven mos in a row.

223
00:13:21,401 --> 00:13:23,670
Your pieces cleared the board, sir.

224
00:13:23,736 --> 00:13:26,172
And with that, the Yut Nori final

225
00:13:26,239 --> 00:13:29,208
is a perfect win for Hadurok-ri!

226
00:13:29,275 --> 00:13:30,443
Is this for real?

227
00:13:30,510 --> 00:13:32,779
Cheers!

228
00:13:33,680 --> 00:13:36,816
Wow, everyone, you did
an amazing job in the first half!

229
00:13:36,883 --> 00:13:38,351
If we keep this up,

230
00:13:38,418 --> 00:13:40,853
it's a win, a total win! Don't worry.

231
00:13:40,920 --> 00:13:42,755
Come on, now, let's toast again!

232
00:13:42,822 --> 00:13:45,525
-Cheers!

233
00:13:45,591 --> 00:13:49,062
Still, all the big-point events
are packed into the second half.

234
00:13:49,128 --> 00:13:50,997
-Stay on your toes, got it?
-Sure.

235
00:13:51,064 --> 00:13:53,299
Come on, the tide has already

236
00:13:53,366 --> 00:13:55,368
turned completely our way, boom!

237
00:13:55,435 --> 00:13:57,603
Don't worry about it.

238
00:13:57,670 --> 00:13:59,072
Honey.

239
00:13:59,138 --> 00:14:01,007
Hey, honey.

240
00:14:01,841 --> 00:14:03,609
Have some gimbap first.

241
00:14:03,676 --> 00:14:05,511
Gimbap?

242
00:14:05,578 --> 00:14:08,848
Surely you didn't make
that gimbap yourself, did you?

243
00:14:08,915 --> 00:14:11,517
No, no, I made it myself.

244
00:14:12,752 --> 00:14:14,887
We already have plenty to eat here.

245
00:14:14,954 --> 00:14:17,323
Why did you make gimbap yourself, huh?

246
00:14:17,390 --> 00:14:20,226
I should do my part to help too.

247
00:14:21,961 --> 00:14:24,297
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

248
00:14:24,364 --> 00:14:26,599
-Here you go.
-Thank you so much.

249
00:14:27,233 --> 00:14:29,402
Enjoy the food, everyone.

250
00:14:29,469 --> 00:14:30,770
Right, sure.

251
00:14:30,837 --> 00:14:33,239
-Would you like two?
-No, no, I have enough.

252
00:14:33,306 --> 00:14:35,675
What's with them? Ugh, jeez!

253
00:14:35,742 --> 00:14:37,577
What, what? What's wrong?

254
00:14:38,144 --> 00:14:40,313
I… I made eye contact with something.

255
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:43,049
How could gimbap make eye contact…

256
00:14:47,387 --> 00:14:49,989
It's eel! Eel.

257
00:14:50,056 --> 00:14:53,292
For stamina, they say eel is the best!

258
00:14:55,294 --> 00:14:56,295
What is this?

259
00:14:57,263 --> 00:15:00,299
Did you see that? It moved.

260
00:15:00,366 --> 00:15:01,968
The gimbap.

261
00:15:03,469 --> 00:15:05,138
It moved.

262
00:15:14,747 --> 00:15:16,616
What, what, what, what!

263
00:15:18,017 --> 00:15:19,218
Live octopus!

264
00:15:19,285 --> 00:15:22,455
They say one octopus makes
even a sick cow jump right up!

265
00:15:22,522 --> 00:15:25,324
Eat up and power up. You have to win!

266
00:15:26,759 --> 00:15:29,061
Come on, go ahead and eat. Eat up!

267
