515
00:31:43,235 --> 00:31:46,071
-Right, Min-gi?
-Register our address?

516
00:31:46,138 --> 00:31:48,140
You registered your address, right?

517
00:31:48,206 --> 00:31:50,108
Oh, of course you did. You did.

518
00:31:50,842 --> 00:31:52,244
Did you do it?

519
00:31:53,111 --> 00:31:54,346
That's your job, dude.

520
00:31:54,413 --> 00:31:56,681
-Did you?
-You should've done it.

521
00:31:56,748 --> 00:32:00,619
Don't tell me you didn't
register your address?

522
00:32:00,685 --> 00:32:03,588
I mean, we're going back up
in three months.

523
00:32:03,655 --> 00:32:06,191
Do we have to register
our address or whatever?

524
00:32:09,828 --> 00:32:11,663
Hey, you total half-wit!

525
00:32:11,730 --> 00:32:14,199
You really didn't register?
You crazy bastard!

526
00:32:14,266 --> 00:32:16,134
Come on, you should've told me!

527
00:32:19,237 --> 00:32:22,040
I have an announcement to make.

528
00:32:22,107 --> 00:32:24,109
Due to having ineligible players,

529
00:32:24,176 --> 00:32:26,878
unfortunately, Hadurok-ri
has been disqualified.

530
00:32:29,347 --> 00:32:32,884
Therefore, the winner of
the 25th Soul-myeon Sports Day

531
00:32:32,951 --> 00:32:35,620
is Sangdurok-ri!

532
00:32:35,687 --> 00:32:36,888
SANGDUROK-RI
HADUROK-RI

533
00:32:41,159 --> 00:32:42,928
Seriously, why did you do that?

534
00:32:44,162 --> 00:32:46,498
No, I said you can't! Oh, no!

535
00:32:48,233 --> 00:32:50,569
We won!

536
00:32:51,403 --> 00:32:54,039
No way. No way.

537
00:33:31,276 --> 00:33:32,844
Hey, get up.

538
00:33:33,845 --> 00:33:36,915
Unbelievable. I said get up!

539
00:33:38,149 --> 00:33:40,519
Hey, get up, get up.

540
00:33:41,086 --> 00:33:42,153
Why…

541
00:33:42,220 --> 00:33:45,156
The sun rose hours ago.
What are you still doing here?

542
00:33:56,635 --> 00:33:58,770
I was about to pack my bags anyway.

543
00:33:58,837 --> 00:34:02,507
Pack later. Don't you know it's Monday?

544
00:34:02,574 --> 00:34:04,476
Hurry up and come out.

545
00:34:06,611 --> 00:34:08,146
Huh?

546
00:34:08,813 --> 00:34:10,448
What about Monday?

547
00:34:12,851 --> 00:34:16,788
What's going on so early again? Geez…

548
00:34:18,089 --> 00:34:19,824
I'm so sleepy I could die.

549
00:34:23,929 --> 00:34:25,997
You punks have no discipline.

550
00:34:26,064 --> 00:34:29,200
All the village elders are here,
and you show up late?

551
00:34:29,267 --> 00:34:31,536
What do you mean we're late?

552
00:34:31,603 --> 00:34:34,839
Our whole village gathers
every Monday morning to exercise.

553
00:34:34,906 --> 00:34:38,176
So from now on, don't be late,
and show up right on the dot.

554
00:34:38,243 --> 00:34:41,379
If you're late from now on,
you'll die by my own hands!

555
00:34:41,446 --> 00:34:43,648
Wait, "from now on"?

556
00:34:44,215 --> 00:34:48,687
Um, then we're not getting kicked out?

557
00:34:48,753 --> 00:34:51,723
Of course, I tried really hard
to kick you guys out.

558
00:34:51,790 --> 00:34:55,427
But unfortunately,
the village elders here

559
00:34:55,493 --> 00:34:59,464
said to just forgive you guys
since you've worked so hard.

560
00:35:01,232 --> 00:35:03,802
But only till the cabbage harvest ends.

561
00:35:03,868 --> 00:35:06,771
-Got it?
-Yes, of course!

562
00:35:06,838 --> 00:35:09,240
Yun-hui, thanks so much! Thank you!

563
00:35:09,307 --> 00:35:11,376
Wait, no. To all the elders,

564
00:35:11,443 --> 00:35:13,244
thank you, thank you so much!

565
00:35:13,311 --> 00:35:14,779
Do well now, do even better.

566
00:35:14,846 --> 00:35:17,616
Line up or leave. Do one or the other!

567
00:35:17,682 --> 00:35:19,918
Yes, sir. We'll be on our way.

568
00:35:19,985 --> 00:35:22,020
We'll work really hard!

569
00:35:22,988 --> 00:35:26,491
But Yun-hui, what happened
to your Village Head position?

570
00:35:26,558 --> 00:35:29,894
A promise is a promise. I stepped down.

571
00:35:30,795 --> 00:35:34,532
But I got re-elected in another vote.

572
00:35:34,599 --> 00:35:36,334
I won by a landslide.

573
00:35:36,401 --> 00:35:37,869
That's great news!

574
00:35:37,936 --> 00:35:39,904
Enough with the useless chatter.

575
00:35:39,971 --> 00:35:41,539
Let's just exercise already.

576
00:35:41,606 --> 00:35:43,541
Hey, you guys get in line too.

577
00:35:44,476 --> 00:35:45,610
Let's get started!

578
00:35:46,578 --> 00:35:47,646
Wow.

579
00:35:47,712 --> 00:35:50,482
Hey, was this town always this pretty?

580
00:35:50,548 --> 00:35:53,585
Right? The view's killer, just killer.

581
00:35:53,652 --> 00:35:56,921
It's nice not worrying now
about getting kicked out to Seoul.

582
00:35:57,956 --> 00:35:59,991
We've pretty much plowed the field.

583
00:36:00,058 --> 00:36:02,227
Our work is already half done.

584
00:36:02,293 --> 00:36:04,529
Our hard times are over. All over!

585
00:36:04,596 --> 00:36:06,431
The end.

586
00:36:07,032 --> 00:36:08,633
Why are you all smiles today?

587
00:36:08,700 --> 00:36:10,335
Su-yeon clapped for him,

588
00:36:10,402 --> 00:36:13,571
so he's totally hyped up
and giggling all day long.

589
00:36:13,638 --> 00:36:15,640
That's not it, you punk! Stop it!

590
00:36:15,707 --> 00:36:18,410
Oh, yes it is. Are you that happy?

591
00:36:18,476 --> 00:36:20,912
No, it's not like that, come on…

592
00:36:22,547 --> 00:36:24,883
Hey, Ki-jun, our sister-in-law is here.

593
00:36:26,451 --> 00:36:27,986
Sister-in-law, my foot.

594
00:36:28,053 --> 00:36:30,288
Seriously, isn't it time you stopped?

595
00:36:30,355 --> 00:36:32,357
Hello there, sister-in-law.

596
00:36:34,559 --> 00:36:35,794
What is it this time?

597
00:36:35,860 --> 00:36:38,463
It's nothing much.
I went to pick mountain herbs,

598
00:36:38,530 --> 00:36:40,632
saw some cliff honey, and got a bit.

599
00:36:40,699 --> 00:36:42,000
Cliff honey?

600
00:36:42,067 --> 00:36:45,236
The wild honey only found
on the edge of sheer cliffs?

601
00:36:45,303 --> 00:36:48,606
Yes, I do a bit of rock climbing.

602
00:36:48,673 --> 00:36:51,209
Wow, you really do it all.

603
00:36:51,276 --> 00:36:52,844
That stuff is insanely rare.

604
00:36:52,911 --> 00:36:53,945
-Oh, really?
-Yes.

605
00:36:54,012 --> 00:36:55,847
Hey, let's try some first.

606
00:36:57,282 --> 00:36:59,784
I don't need this junk. Take it back.

607
00:37:00,552 --> 00:37:03,988
You doing this is way too much
and makes me so uncomfortable.

608
00:37:04,055 --> 00:37:07,459
I was just so grateful
and sorry you saved me last time…

609
00:37:07,525 --> 00:37:09,828
Enough. I already forgot all about it.

610
00:37:09,894 --> 00:37:11,830
No need to feel grateful or sorry.

611
00:37:11,896 --> 00:37:14,666
So never come looking for me again.

612
00:37:14,733 --> 00:37:16,301
And don't worry about me.

613
00:37:16,367 --> 00:37:19,270
Pretend you don't see me,
and don't even talk to me.

614
00:37:19,337 --> 00:37:20,939
Do you understand?

615
00:37:28,947 --> 00:37:32,550
-Hey, you could've just taken it.
-Why are you being so dramatic?

616
00:37:32,617 --> 00:37:33,885
She meant well.

617
00:37:33,952 --> 00:37:35,653
Right, you went too far, man.

618
00:37:35,720 --> 00:37:38,790
Whatever. It's the only way
she'll stop bothering me.

619
00:37:45,663 --> 00:37:49,534
Never in my life did I think
I'd buy this many cabbage seeds

620
00:37:49,601 --> 00:37:52,504
with my own money, jeez.

621
00:37:53,505 --> 00:37:55,406
Sir, what should we do first?

622
00:37:55,473 --> 00:37:57,408
You ordered without knowing that?

623
00:37:57,475 --> 00:38:00,078
This is our first time farming, sir.

624
00:38:00,145 --> 00:38:03,148
It's not that hard. Listen up.

625
00:38:03,214 --> 00:38:07,252
First, put potting soil in these trays.

626
00:38:07,318 --> 00:38:09,954
Plant two or three seeds in each hole.

627
00:38:10,822 --> 00:38:12,357
How deep?

628
00:38:12,423 --> 00:38:15,727
Not too deep,
not too shallow, just right.

629
00:38:15,794 --> 00:38:20,665
Then, when the soil looks dry,
just go ahead and water them.

630
00:38:20,732 --> 00:38:21,833
How much?

631
00:38:21,900 --> 00:38:24,969
Not too much,
not too little, just right.

632
00:38:25,036 --> 00:38:28,840
Then, once the seedlings get
not too big, not too small,

633
00:38:28,907 --> 00:38:30,775
and look grown just right,

634
00:38:30,842 --> 00:38:33,511
give the field fungicide
and compound fertilizer,

635
00:38:33,578 --> 00:38:35,146
and make furrows and ridges.

636
00:38:35,213 --> 00:38:37,849
Then, on the ridges,
not too big, not too small,

637
00:38:37,916 --> 00:38:39,684
make holes that are just right,

638
00:38:39,751 --> 00:38:41,419
and just plant the seedlings.

639
00:38:41,486 --> 00:38:44,022
Then, as you water them
and pull the weeds,

640
00:38:44,088 --> 00:38:45,323
these guys will grow.

641
00:38:45,390 --> 00:38:48,593
Then take a good look
and thin out the scrawny ones.

642
00:38:48,660 --> 00:38:52,831
Then, if these guys aren't growing,
top-dress with compound fertilizer.

643
00:38:52,897 --> 00:38:55,533
If bugs appear,
gently douse them with pesticide.

644
00:38:55,600 --> 00:38:57,869
Then, before the frost hits,

645
00:38:57,936 --> 00:38:59,771
tie them up tightly with string.

646
00:38:59,838 --> 00:39:03,107
Then, once they're plump
and packed full on the inside,

647
00:39:03,174 --> 00:39:06,644
take a knife to the cabbage base,
not too hard, not too soft,

648
00:39:06,711 --> 00:39:09,848
chop it off just right, and that's it.

649
00:39:09,914 --> 00:39:11,216
Easy, right?

650
00:39:12,083 --> 00:39:16,054
Call if you need anything else.
I'm just really busy right now.

651
00:39:16,120 --> 00:39:18,389
-Good luck.
-Um, sir! Sir!

652
00:39:18,456 --> 00:39:20,792
-Sure, good luck.
-Hey.

653
00:39:20,859 --> 00:39:23,895
That was Korean just now, right?

654
00:39:23,962 --> 00:39:25,663
Just enough…

655
00:39:25,730 --> 00:39:29,801
Why is growing cabbages
so deep and mysterious?

656
00:39:29,868 --> 00:39:31,135
My head hurts.

657
00:39:31,202 --> 00:39:33,238
I'm so hungry, so hungry.

658
00:39:44,115 --> 00:39:46,050
Ramen again?

659
00:39:46,117 --> 00:39:47,852
Where are your aunt and uncle?

660
00:39:47,919 --> 00:39:49,754
Want some?

661
00:39:49,821 --> 00:39:51,856
My uncle's at the clinic.

662
00:39:51,923 --> 00:39:54,058
As he fed the cow,
its tail hit his eye.

663
00:39:55,193 --> 00:39:57,095
A cow's tail hit him in the eye?

664
00:39:57,161 --> 00:39:59,597
Is your uncle always that unlucky?

665
00:40:00,231 --> 00:40:03,635
My uncle does have unusually bad luck.

666
00:40:06,104 --> 00:40:09,607
Oh, right. Do you know
how to plant cabbage seedlings?

667
00:40:09,674 --> 00:40:11,576
Why? Didn't the seller tell you?

668
00:40:11,643 --> 00:40:15,680
He explained it,
but I couldn't understand it at all.

669
00:40:15,747 --> 00:40:20,084
Well, it depends on the soil
and the type of cabbage seed.

670
00:40:20,151 --> 00:40:22,820
Depending on what compost
and fertilizer you use,

671
00:40:22,887 --> 00:40:24,789
the method changes completely.

672
00:40:24,856 --> 00:40:27,125
So there's no single right answer.

673
00:40:28,126 --> 00:40:29,427
Just do your research.

674
00:40:29,494 --> 00:40:31,529
One wrong move ruins a year's crop.

675
00:40:32,563 --> 00:40:34,832
What? Ruin our whole crop?

676
00:40:34,899 --> 00:40:37,368
Once, I gave them too much water,

677
00:40:37,435 --> 00:40:39,704
and every single seedling died.

678
00:40:39,771 --> 00:40:41,205
We can't let that happen.

679
00:40:41,272 --> 00:40:43,308
Can't you show us how to plant them?

680
00:40:43,374 --> 00:40:46,577
I haven't grown much cabbage,
so I don't really know.

681
00:40:49,247 --> 00:40:51,983
There is one surefire way, though…

682
00:40:53,318 --> 00:40:56,287
-What is it?
-Go pay him a visit.

683
00:40:56,354 --> 00:40:58,589
He raises any crop in any condition

684
00:40:58,656 --> 00:41:01,092
to grade A+++.
Our village's Farming God!

685
00:41:02,327 --> 00:41:05,096
The Farming God? Who's that?

686
00:41:09,400 --> 00:41:11,970
Forget it. Go ask somewhere else.

687
00:41:12,036 --> 00:41:14,839
Why would I do you a favor
and teach you that?

688
00:41:16,507 --> 00:41:19,143
Don't be like that, sir.
Please just teach us.

689
00:41:19,210 --> 00:41:21,112
I have a mountain of work myself.

690
00:41:21,179 --> 00:41:23,748
Besides, it took me
a lifetime to learn,

691
00:41:23,815 --> 00:41:25,683
and you want to snag it for free?

692
00:41:25,750 --> 00:41:29,654
Did you steal Scrooge's underwear,
you shameless bastards?

693
00:41:30,989 --> 00:41:33,558
We'll help with your work in return.

694
00:41:33,624 --> 00:41:36,728
We'll do anything you tell us to do.

695
00:41:36,794 --> 00:41:40,732
Is that so?
You'll do anything I tell you to do?

696
00:41:46,070 --> 00:41:47,739
This smell, seriously!

697
00:41:47,805 --> 00:41:50,708
Why is that guy the Farming God?
I'm losing my mind!

698
00:41:50,775 --> 00:41:52,910
Hey, just keep cleaning.

699
00:41:52,977 --> 00:41:55,446
He said he's coming to inspect it.

700
00:41:55,513 --> 00:41:59,283
At least we're better off than Ki-jun.

701
00:42:00,852 --> 00:42:02,787
They always make me do this stuff!

702
00:42:02,854 --> 00:42:04,122
Isn't he better off?

703
00:42:04,188 --> 00:42:05,790
We're better off. Hurry up.

704
00:42:05,857 --> 00:42:09,027
Still, this smell is driving me crazy.

705
00:42:13,331 --> 00:42:15,233
Guys, Mom says to eat watermelon!

706
00:42:15,299 --> 00:42:17,035
-Watermelon!

707
00:42:17,101 --> 00:42:19,904
-Watermelon, watermelon!
-No way!

708
00:42:26,377 --> 00:42:29,313
Watermelon, watermelon!

709
00:42:30,114 --> 00:42:34,485
Guys! You could've taken me with you!

710
00:42:36,854 --> 00:42:38,489
The ladder!

711
00:42:38,556 --> 00:42:39,891
Guys! Wait, wait!

712
00:42:39,957 --> 00:42:42,760
Hey, hey! The ladder!

713
00:42:43,594 --> 00:42:46,130
Hurry up and bring it over.

714
00:42:46,664 --> 00:42:47,532
Have some.

715
00:42:47,598 --> 00:42:49,534
-Thank you so much.
-Thank you.

716
00:42:49,600 --> 00:42:50,768
Thank you.

717
00:42:52,036 --> 00:42:53,371
How is it? Is it sweet?

718
00:42:54,305 --> 00:42:56,808
Yes, it's so sweet. It's pure sugar!

719
00:42:56,874 --> 00:43:00,745
By the way, sir, your house
is really nice and luxurious.

720
00:43:02,080 --> 00:43:05,116
When will you teach us
how to plant cabbage seedlings?

721
00:43:05,183 --> 00:43:06,751
You're far from ready.

722
00:43:06,818 --> 00:43:08,820
You only did a tiny bit of work.

723
00:43:08,886 --> 00:43:10,288
Do more work. More, more!

724
00:43:10,354 --> 00:43:12,590
Of course, sir. We should do more.

725
00:43:12,657 --> 00:43:14,725
You had to say something pointless.

726
00:43:16,794 --> 00:43:19,230
That must be
your college graduation photo.

727
00:43:19,897 --> 00:43:22,133
-My brother's a high school grad.
-Oh.

728
00:43:22,200 --> 00:43:24,202
So it's from high school graduation.

729
00:43:24,268 --> 00:43:25,903
No, middle school.

730
00:43:26,671 --> 00:43:28,005
-What?

731
00:43:28,072 --> 00:43:31,075
That was you in middle school?

732
00:43:31,142 --> 00:43:33,344
Man-gu's looked like that since birth.

733
00:43:33,411 --> 00:43:35,179
No one looked that old so young.

734
00:43:35,246 --> 00:43:38,850
The doctor who delivered him
almost bowed to him in respect.

735
00:43:39,617 --> 00:43:43,020
Mom, why embarrass me
in front of these guys?

736
00:43:45,089 --> 00:43:46,858
Don't laugh.

737
00:43:46,924 --> 00:43:49,260
-Don't laugh, you punks!
-What's wrong?

738
00:43:49,327 --> 00:43:51,729
What's wrong with his face?
My husband's cute.

739
00:43:52,663 --> 00:43:54,599
You're so cute.

740
00:43:54,665 --> 00:43:58,169
Have you no manners?
How dare you touch your husband's face?

741
00:43:58,236 --> 00:44:00,037
Sorry, Mother.

742
00:44:00,805 --> 00:44:02,039
You're so cute.

743
00:44:02,106 --> 00:44:03,441
Why, that…

744
00:44:03,508 --> 00:44:04,976
Why? Not his butt either?

745
00:44:05,042 --> 00:44:07,178
-No, my butt's fine!
-He says I can.

746
00:44:07,245 --> 00:44:09,647
-Why, that little…
-Mom, hold it in.

747
00:44:09,714 --> 00:44:12,583
Talking to her will just upset you.

748
00:44:14,118 --> 00:44:15,486
Wait.

749
00:44:16,154 --> 00:44:18,356
Don't you think we forgot something?

750
00:44:19,023 --> 00:44:20,057
-Huh?

751
00:44:22,727 --> 00:44:24,028
-There's nothing.
-Nope.

752
00:44:24,095 --> 00:44:25,296
There isn't, right?

753
00:44:27,465 --> 00:44:29,967
Hey! Min-gi!

754
00:44:31,068 --> 00:44:33,337
Over here! Over here!

755
00:44:34,105 --> 00:44:35,239
Han-cheol…

756
00:44:36,007 --> 00:44:37,542
Hey, you jerks!

757
00:44:37,608 --> 00:44:40,511
Where did you all go without me?

758
00:44:41,712 --> 00:44:44,415
I'm dying to pee. What do I do?

759
00:44:49,720 --> 00:44:51,022
Huh?

760
00:44:51,088 --> 00:44:53,524
It doesn't look as high as I thought.

761
00:44:53,591 --> 00:44:55,760
Should I just jump down?

762
00:44:57,361 --> 00:44:59,764
I don't think I can do it, darn it.

763
00:45:01,032 --> 00:45:02,700
Oh!

764
00:45:14,745 --> 00:45:17,048
Jeez, here goes nothing.

765
00:45:17,882 --> 00:45:21,018
If I fall, I die. If I fall, I die.

766
00:45:24,889 --> 00:45:26,057
Wait, what?

767
00:45:26,123 --> 00:45:27,959
It was only this far?

768
00:45:28,025 --> 00:45:30,228
Ha, I got scared for nothing.

769
00:45:30,294 --> 00:45:32,597
Let's do this in one go like a man.

770
00:45:32,663 --> 00:45:36,033
One, two, three!

771
00:45:39,870 --> 00:45:42,573
Why did my pants get stuck right here?

772
00:45:45,843 --> 00:45:49,280
Help me! Please help me!

773
00:45:54,151 --> 00:45:55,953
Excuse me, is anyone there?

774
00:45:58,356 --> 00:46:00,591
Please help! Is nobody around?

775
00:46:00,658 --> 00:46:01,859
I'm about to pee!

776
00:46:01,926 --> 00:46:04,895
Please help! Ma'am! Auntie, auntie!

777
00:46:15,206 --> 00:46:17,775
Wait, how can you just leave, Bul-ja?

778
00:46:18,843 --> 00:46:21,512
Didn't you say to ignore you
and not talk to you?

779
00:46:21,579 --> 00:46:23,881
Um… That's true, but not right now.

780
00:46:23,948 --> 00:46:27,184
This is an emergency! A real emergency!

781
00:46:27,251 --> 00:46:29,220
So please help me.

782
00:46:29,287 --> 00:46:30,921
I really have to pee.

783
00:46:35,893 --> 00:46:37,762
It's stuck in the back, the back.

784
00:46:38,529 --> 00:46:40,731
Please hurry, hurry up!

785
00:46:41,899 --> 00:46:44,001
It's coming out! It's coming! Ahh!

786
00:46:46,437 --> 00:46:48,906
I'm so embarrassed right now…

787
00:46:52,176 --> 00:46:55,212
Goodness! What are you two doing here?

788
00:46:55,279 --> 00:46:59,250
What are you up to? Are you two dating?

789
00:47:06,891 --> 00:47:08,626
Goodbye, sister-in-law.

790
00:47:10,594 --> 00:47:12,797
It was an accident! It's not like that!

791
00:47:12,863 --> 00:47:14,665
-An accident!
-Caught red-handed!

792
00:47:14,732 --> 00:47:15,800
Why play innocent?

793
00:47:15,866 --> 00:47:17,835
It's true! I got stuck right here.

794
00:47:17,902 --> 00:47:20,971
She freed me and we fell.
Really, it was an accident!

795
00:47:21,038 --> 00:47:24,342
Look at this punk making excuses.

796
00:47:24,408 --> 00:47:27,478
You sure live up to your fame
as a foreign lady-killer.

797
00:47:27,545 --> 00:47:29,714
That's old news!
It's a misunderstanding!

798
00:47:29,780 --> 00:47:32,616
Around that woman,
nothing goes right, nothing.

799
00:47:32,683 --> 00:47:34,885
Well, I'll be on my way now.

800
00:47:38,322 --> 00:47:39,957
Take care, ma'am.

801
00:47:40,024 --> 00:47:42,360
You're doomed.
There goes the loudspeaker.

802
00:47:42,426 --> 00:47:44,695
Isn't that guy going way too far?

803
00:47:44,762 --> 00:47:47,865
After working us this hard,
shouldn't he tell us by now?

804
00:47:47,932 --> 00:47:52,136
Still, our Ki-jun filmed a bed scene
during all that. I'm so jealous.

805
00:47:53,504 --> 00:47:55,373
Seriously, cut it out, damn it!

806
00:47:56,374 --> 00:47:57,975
How valiant.

807
00:47:58,042 --> 00:47:59,677
What about you, Han-cheol?

808
00:47:59,744 --> 00:48:02,079
Your image is restored.
Won't you confess?

809
00:48:02,146 --> 00:48:03,347
Confess?

810
00:48:04,014 --> 00:48:06,584
Not yet. I'm not ready to confess…

811
00:48:07,351 --> 00:48:09,887
Hey, did she say she has no boyfriend?

812
00:48:09,954 --> 00:48:12,323
I bet she has a boyfriend.

813
00:48:12,390 --> 00:48:15,659
-A boyfriend?
-True, a woman that pretty

814
00:48:15,726 --> 00:48:17,561
is bound to have a boyfriend.

815
00:48:17,628 --> 00:48:19,263
Of course she does, man.

816
00:48:19,330 --> 00:48:22,533
She's pretty, innocent,
and has a great figure.

817
00:48:22,600 --> 00:48:24,902
I bet she's super popular.

818
00:48:31,342 --> 00:48:32,510
He panicked! Panicked!

819
00:48:32,576 --> 00:48:35,813
Look at the way he runs.
Like his ass is on fire!

820
00:48:35,880 --> 00:48:37,481
How can people be like that?

821
00:48:37,548 --> 00:48:39,717
Is teasing people that much fun?

822
00:48:43,821 --> 00:48:45,956
-Yes! I live for this now!
-Yes!

823
00:48:46,023 --> 00:48:48,058
I live for this fun too!

824
00:49:02,039 --> 00:49:04,241
What if she really has a boyfriend?

825
00:49:04,308 --> 00:49:05,709
That can't happen.

826
00:49:05,776 --> 00:49:08,345
I can't just go up and ask her.

827
00:49:11,315 --> 00:49:12,716
That's right!

828
00:49:12,783 --> 00:49:15,853
If she has a boyfriend,
she'll have a ring. A ring.

829
00:49:20,524 --> 00:49:22,660
I'm too far away to see clearly.

830
00:49:29,266 --> 00:49:31,035
I'm so sleepy.

831
00:49:31,702 --> 00:49:35,005
I got no sleep shoveling all night.

832
00:49:35,072 --> 00:49:38,375
I do morning exercises, paint all day,

833
00:49:38,442 --> 00:49:40,678
and get dragged to Sports Day.

834
00:49:40,744 --> 00:49:43,614
What country town has this much work?

835
00:49:47,218 --> 00:49:48,986
I should get some rest.

836
00:49:58,963 --> 00:50:00,664
She's asleep, she's asleep.

837
00:50:00,731 --> 00:50:03,901
Okay, now's my chance.

838
00:50:50,548 --> 00:50:53,450
What are you doing right now?

839
00:50:54,351 --> 00:50:55,719
Pardon?

840
00:50:55,786 --> 00:51:00,391
Wow, this painting is pure art!

841
00:51:00,457 --> 00:51:04,528
Are these chrysanthemums?
And the people look so real. Here!

842
00:51:04,595 --> 00:51:05,996
-Excuse me?
-A high five!

843
00:51:06,063 --> 00:51:07,998
To cheer you on. Keep it up!

844
00:51:08,065 --> 00:51:09,533
Here we go!

845
00:51:10,200 --> 00:51:11,702
The other hand too!

846
00:51:11,769 --> 00:51:13,170
Yes!

847
00:51:15,406 --> 00:51:18,409
Keep up the good work. Thank you!

848
00:51:29,787 --> 00:51:31,956
What's with that nutjob?

849
00:51:33,324 --> 00:51:36,660
Seriously, this town
wears me out in so many ways.

850
00:51:41,265 --> 00:51:44,335
Why do you keep grinning so creepily?

851
00:51:45,235 --> 00:51:47,771
You know, I think that woman's single.

852
00:51:47,838 --> 00:51:50,107
She didn't have a ring on her hand.

853
00:51:52,943 --> 00:51:55,980
Really? But…

854
00:51:56,046 --> 00:51:58,749
does no ring mean no boyfriend?

855
00:51:58,816 --> 00:52:01,685
People barely wear couple rings now.

856
00:52:01,752 --> 00:52:05,422
Right, who's tacky enough
to wear couple rings these days?

857
00:52:08,258 --> 00:52:11,495
Really? That's not good.

858
00:52:11,562 --> 00:52:13,697
She really can't have a boyfriend.

859
00:52:18,002 --> 00:52:19,737
Are you back?

860
00:52:19,803 --> 00:52:20,971
Yes.

861
00:52:21,038 --> 00:52:23,340
Oh, are you all right?

862
00:52:23,407 --> 00:52:25,676
How did a cow's tail hit your eye?

863
00:52:25,743 --> 00:52:27,945
Boy, when you're out of luck,

864
00:52:28,012 --> 00:52:30,648
all kinds of crazy things happen.

865
00:52:30,714 --> 00:52:32,049
Oh, by the way,

866
00:52:32,116 --> 00:52:33,851
I heard you're dating Bul-ja?

867
00:52:34,485 --> 00:52:35,853
Congratulations!

868
00:52:35,919 --> 00:52:38,689
You just moved down here,
and you're already dating?

869
00:52:38,756 --> 00:52:40,190
What does time matter?

870
00:52:40,257 --> 00:52:42,426
Wait, what do you mean? Who said that?

871
00:52:42,493 --> 00:52:43,894
That's what Sun-bun said.

872
00:52:43,961 --> 00:52:45,663
You two rolled around hugging?

873
00:52:45,729 --> 00:52:47,731
If it was Sun-bun…

874
00:52:48,365 --> 00:52:51,335
I swear, that woman…
Anyway, it's not like that, sir.

875
00:52:51,402 --> 00:52:52,670
It's a misunderstanding.

876
00:52:52,736 --> 00:52:54,672
I'm home.

877
00:52:54,738 --> 00:52:57,041
I heard Bul-ja is having your baby?

878
00:52:57,741 --> 00:53:00,277
What? A baby?

879
00:53:00,344 --> 00:53:02,012
A little baby?

880
00:53:02,079 --> 00:53:03,747
Wow.

881
00:53:04,748 --> 00:53:05,916
That's how it starts.

882
00:53:05,983 --> 00:53:08,352
-Let's go inside.
-Yes, go on in.

883
00:53:08,419 --> 00:53:10,054
Hey, congratulations!

884
00:53:10,120 --> 00:53:12,890
-They're that close now?
-Wow, that's really fast.

885
00:53:12,956 --> 00:53:14,792
Right, it's true. It's all true.

886
00:53:14,858 --> 00:53:17,327
Hey, little rock star. Just got home?

887
00:53:17,394 --> 00:53:20,931
Hi. Wait, what's wrong with this?

888
00:53:20,998 --> 00:53:23,434
Hold on, what happened to this?

889
00:53:24,368 --> 00:53:26,103
I fell on my way home.

890
00:53:26,937 --> 00:53:29,039
That's a lie. If you just fell,

891
00:53:29,106 --> 00:53:31,108
how could it be cut so cleanly?

892
00:53:32,943 --> 00:53:35,579
Someone clearly cut this
on purpose with a knife.

893
00:53:35,646 --> 00:53:36,947
I had this done to me.

894
00:53:37,014 --> 00:53:38,582
Were you an outcast?

895
00:53:39,516 --> 00:53:41,852
Anyway, someone did this on purpose.

896
00:53:41,919 --> 00:53:44,688
-It's not like that.
-Of course it is.

897
00:53:44,755 --> 00:53:46,590
Which punk did this? Tell me.

898
00:53:46,657 --> 00:53:48,058
I'll teach them a lesson.

899
00:53:48,125 --> 00:53:51,361
Min-ho, give me your bag
and go wash up. I'll sew it up.

900
00:53:55,599 --> 00:53:57,468
Do you actually believe him?

901
00:53:57,534 --> 00:53:59,937
He's 100% getting bullied.

902
00:54:00,003 --> 00:54:01,872
The kid said he just fell.

903
00:54:01,939 --> 00:54:04,575
It's not your business,
so you stay out of it.

904
00:54:06,677 --> 00:54:09,046
Is that woman really his mom?

905
00:54:09,113 --> 00:54:10,380
What is wrong with her?

906
00:54:10,447 --> 00:54:12,049
She must have her reasons.

907
00:54:12,116 --> 00:54:14,118
I'm late! I'm late!

908
00:54:16,854 --> 00:54:19,223
-Hi, guys!
-Hi, where are you going?

909
00:54:19,289 --> 00:54:22,392
I have a part-time job. See you!

910
00:54:23,660 --> 00:54:25,095
A part-time job?

911
00:54:25,162 --> 00:54:27,264
What part-time job in this backwater?

912
00:54:27,331 --> 00:54:28,932
HADUROK-RI 7

913
00:54:55,092 --> 00:54:58,262
Hello, I'm Matilda!

914
00:55:00,597 --> 00:55:03,901
I had spaghetti for dinner tonight.

915
00:55:07,271 --> 00:55:08,605
Aglio e olio.

916
00:55:11,441 --> 00:55:14,611
But I kept thinking of someone.

917
00:55:17,414 --> 00:55:18,882
Who could it be?

918
00:55:23,453 --> 00:55:24,888
It was all of you!

919
00:55:30,060 --> 00:55:33,197
Matilda's music show will now begin.

920
00:55:39,336 --> 00:55:43,307
Red Riding Psycho and Wizard of OMG,
good to see you both!

921
00:55:48,045 --> 00:55:50,747
Welcome, Pollack Roe Conan!

922
00:55:57,654 --> 00:56:00,591
Charisma Hong, 100 flower balloons!

923
00:56:00,657 --> 00:56:03,293
Thank you so much! Thank you!

924
00:56:07,364 --> 00:56:10,500
Charisma Hong, you requested a song.

925
00:56:10,567 --> 00:56:13,570
This song again?
You must really love this song.

926
00:56:25,015 --> 00:56:26,350
Dad.

927
00:56:28,352 --> 00:56:30,220
I was practicing. Singing practice.

928
00:56:34,858 --> 00:56:38,061
Lady Gaga.
Don't you know Lady Gaga, Dad?

929
00:56:39,029 --> 00:56:40,564
Right, the stream!

930
00:56:41,298 --> 00:56:44,735
Everyone, I think Matilda's stream
needs to wrap up here.

931
00:56:44,801 --> 00:56:47,504
I'm so sorry. Next week--

932
00:56:56,513 --> 00:56:58,982
No! My hair!

933
00:58:00,944 --> 00:58:03,747
What total humiliation on my stream.

934
00:58:03,814 --> 00:58:07,417
I barely had any hair left to cut,
and he cut it again!

935
00:58:11,121 --> 00:58:13,623
-What are you doing?
-My goodness!

936
00:58:13,690 --> 00:58:16,526
Jeez, you scared me.

937
00:58:17,861 --> 00:58:19,396
Sorry.

938
00:58:19,463 --> 00:58:21,298
But what happened to your hair?

939
00:58:23,467 --> 00:58:25,435
Dad caught me streaming and cut it.

940
00:58:26,103 --> 00:58:28,238
Streaming? What kind of stream?

941
00:58:28,905 --> 00:58:31,041
Just something like that.

942
00:58:32,776 --> 00:58:33,977
I'm going crazy.

943
00:58:34,044 --> 00:58:36,213
How can I go to school like this?

944
00:58:37,848 --> 00:58:39,616
When I become an idol later,

945
00:58:39,683 --> 00:58:41,918
leaked ugly photos will cause a fuss.

946
00:58:48,892 --> 00:58:50,360
Tell me something.

947
00:58:50,427 --> 00:58:52,596
Why do you want to be an idol?

948
00:58:54,164 --> 00:58:58,335
That's the only way to escape
this dead-end country town.

949
00:58:59,603 --> 00:59:01,271
I'm not good at studying.

950
00:59:01,338 --> 00:59:04,341
And it's not like my family has money.

951
00:59:05,075 --> 00:59:08,945
I'm only better than others
at singing and dancing.

952
00:59:10,614 --> 00:59:13,450
But Dad says he's totally against
me being a singer.

953
00:59:13,517 --> 00:59:15,352
-Why?
-I don't know.

954
00:59:15,419 --> 00:59:18,121
He says I can do anything,
just never be a singer.

955
00:59:20,590 --> 00:59:23,827
Then again, with these looks,
I'm trying to be a singer.

956
00:59:23,894 --> 00:59:25,462
No way he wouldn't stop me.

957
00:59:25,529 --> 00:59:27,898
Come on, kid, what do looks matter?

958
00:59:30,067 --> 00:59:32,135
Even you said last time I'd need

959
00:59:32,202 --> 00:59:34,438
plastic surgery first to be an idol.

960
00:59:36,106 --> 00:59:39,609
That was a joke.
Hey, a singer just has to sing well.

961
00:59:39,676 --> 00:59:41,111
What do looks matter?

962
00:59:41,178 --> 00:59:44,581
And what's wrong with your face?
You're plenty cute.

963
00:59:46,716 --> 00:59:49,352
-What?
-When you become an idol later,

964
00:59:49,419 --> 00:59:52,189
you have to give me your autograph.
Got it?

965
00:59:52,255 --> 00:59:53,890
Okay?

966
00:59:55,692 --> 00:59:57,661
You've got this!

967
01:00:47,611 --> 01:00:49,546
She must be upset.

968
01:00:50,847 --> 01:00:52,816
How could she not be?

969
01:00:55,886 --> 01:00:58,054
Should I sew it for her?

970
01:00:59,890 --> 01:01:02,259
Okay, I'll do it for her.
